# The patches tools/common/fetch/fetch-qemu-linux.sh applies to QEMU v10.2.1,
# in order. One file name per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# 0001 (the virtio-gpu-gl reset fix) is not here: it is the Windows build's,
# against 11.1.0, and does not apply to 10.2.1. 0003 is the same fix carried
# to 10.2.1: without it a GTK window on a Wayland host loses its GL context
# to the vCPU thread when the guest resets the card, and its menu bar turns
# transparent or fills with stale pixels.
0002-intel_iommu-honour-CFI-and-block-compatibility-format.patch
0003-virtio-gpu-gl-Disable-scanouts-on-reset-in-the-main-10.2.1.patch
# 0004: with gl=on the GL area has no window of its own, and the cursor QEMU
# hides over the guest was set on the whole window, menu bar and tabs too.
0004-ui-gtk-Set-the-guest-s-cursor-on-the-GL-area-s-own-window.patch
# 0006: -machine x-nazuna=on, the platform as the customer's PC's firmware
# describes it, for run-nazuna (docs/NAZUNA-VM.md). Off, nothing changes.
0006-x86-nazuna-describe-the-platform-as-an-ASUS-B650-board.patch
